{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q412673","formula":"Na₈(Si₆Al₆)O₂₄(SO₄)·H₂O","hill":"Al6H2Na8O29SSi6","elements":["H","O","Na","Al","Si","S"],"composition":{"H":2.0,"O":29.0,"S":1.0,"Al":6.0,"Na":8.0,"Si":6.0},"names":{"en":"Nosean","ru":"Нозеан","uk":"Нозеан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Nosean, also known as noselite, is a mineral of the feldspathoid group with formula: Na8(Al6Si6O24)(SO4)·H2O. It forms isometric crystals of variable color: white, grey, blue, green, to brown. It has a Mohs hardness of 5.5 to 6 and a specific gravity of 2.3 to 2.4. It is fluorescent.","ru":"Нозеан — минерал, алюмосиликат натрия каркасного строения с дополнительным анионом [SO4]2-. Впервые был описан в 1815 году из Рейнской области (Германия). Был назван в честь немецкого минералога К. Нозе (1753-1835).","uk":"Нозеан (рос. нозеан; англ. nosean; нім."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q412673","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nosean","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%B0%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9D%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%B5%D0%B0%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nosean_single_crystal_-_Ochtendung,_Eifel,_Germany.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 nl"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q410759","formula":"Na₄Si₃Al₃O₁₂Cl","names":{"en":"Sodalite","ru":"Содалит","uk":"Содаліт"},"elements":["O","Na","Al","Si","Cl"],"fame":34,"kind":"crystal"},{"id":"Q410447","formula